.TH TIMERC 1 "2026" "timerc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timerc, timerc-bg \- native X11 countdown timer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timerc
[\fItime\fR] [\fItask\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B timerc-bg
[\fItime\fR] [\fItask\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B timerc
runs in the foreground and blocks until the timer finishes (usable in scripts:
\fBtimerc 5m && notify-send done\fR).
.B timerc-bg
is the same program detached from the terminal.
With no arguments an interactive setup screen opens.
.SH TIME FORMATS
25m, 1h30m, 45 (minutes), 30:00, 1:30:00, u15:30 (until clock time).
.SH SWITCHES
Prefix letters before the time: d shutdown, a alert, f/r fullscreen, p pausable,
l lock keyboard/mouse, / sleep mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " alert|shutdown"
Mode when the timer ends.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-pausable
Allow pause/resume.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-fullscreen
Start fullscreen.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-lock
Disconnect USB keyboard/mouse (needs timerc-lock-helper).
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Select a theme.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help.
.SH FILES
~/.config/timerc/ (config.conf, data.db, timer.log)
.SH AUTHOR
Mohamad Almousli <https://al-mo.de>
